<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Old Hittite Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1650 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century-bce">17th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Old Hittite Kingdom was the first phase of Hittite statehood in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, established around 1650 BCE with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> as its capital. Its early kings expanded into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-i">Mursili I</a> raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> around 1595 BCE. Internal strife followed, and the state later developed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-hittite-kingdom">New Hittite Kingdom</a>, the imperial phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/old-hittite-kingdom.jpg" alt="Old Hittite Kingdom" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nissrpska · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hittite_kingdoms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
